  "narrative": {
    "intro": "North Carolina recorded total obligations of $153M in federal contract awards for FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 97.3% year over year. The state received 736 awards with an average award size of $207K. Fiscal-year history shows a sharp drop from multi‑billion-dollar totals in recent years: FY22 was $8.6B, FY23 was $7B, FY24 was $7.2B, FY25 was $9.3B, and FY26 was $5.6B. The Department of Agriculture is the largest buyer so far in FY2027 to date, with obligations of $99.4M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC is the largest vendor, with $99.6M in obligations, and Logging is the largest industry by NAICS with $99.6M. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $38.5M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $5.9M. Other notable agencies include the Environmental Protection Agency with $4.2M and the Department of Justice with $2.4M. Top vendor and industry concentrations show that a few large awards account for a majority of the current-year total.",
    "sections": [
